Well I finally did it! I got to the Wizard. I had everything I 
needed and attacked him (it?) after killing his dog and 
avoiding the level tp trap the dog had been standing on.
When I hit him he disappeared. No problem, I figured, I'd just 
look around for him. I went into the tp trap and ended up on
level 60 (bottom of hell) and there he was. Funny thing though,
he just teleported away every time I swung at him. I found the
way up and there he was waiting for me. I hit him again and again
he disappeared. Well to make a long story short, I chased him up 
a few levels repeating the process ( he never did attack me) and then
I got an error message.

Warning! null at 44 11 Maybe you better quit.

Quit?! Not now!
So I kept playing untill I got a mysteriously unhell-like level
52 and attacked a ghost there. Then I got the second error message...

floating exception

and I was put back into UNIX. I looked real fast and saw the remenants
of my game floating around in the games directory, but it was gone
by the time I looked twice.

*sigh*

Does anyone have any idea what happened? What should I have done at
the first error message? I am playing Unix NetHack Verson 2.2a on 
a SUN system. Is it possible to win in this version or will this
happen every time I go after the Wiz? Email is fine if this info is
not of general interest (I know this is an old version of hack, but
I'm not the system manager...).

